{% extends "_base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Methodology · awesome-private-inference{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<section class="max-w-4xl text-slate-700">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900">How to read the observatory</h1>
  <p class="mt-3">The unit of analysis is a client, model and request route. A brand can have several plaintext paths and different client policies. The <a class="underline" href="./index.html#routes">route cards</a> name the client mode, processes that may receive plaintext, published values, client acceptance and missing evidence.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Three distinct sets</h2>
  <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3 text-sm">
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-3"><strong>Published</strong><p class="mt-1">A provider serves a manifest, allowlist, release or reference history. Our capture retains exact bytes, origin, time and hash. Publication does not authenticate the file or prove deployment.</p></div>
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-3"><strong>Accepted</strong><p class="mt-1">An identified client policy permits a value. A built-in root, automatically refreshed manifest and locally pinned file have different authorities and rollback behavior.</p></div>
    <div class="rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-3"><strong>Observed</strong><p class="mt-1">A particular probe or request received evidence at one time. The check must bind authenticated measurement, recipient key, requested model and actual plaintext path before it supports a route verdict.</p></div>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm">A mismatch may reflect a legitimate rollout, stale client, rejected update or attack. The change event requests review; it does not authorize a value. Reviewer decisions belong in separate signed or witnessed records.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">What the current labels mean</h2>
  <dl class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm">
    {% for outcome, style in outcome_style.items() %}<div class="rounded border border-slate-200 bg-white p-3"><dt class="font-semibold">{{ style[0] }}</dt><dd>{{ style[2] }}</dd></div>{% endfor %}
  </dl>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm">A green adapter field is a result from that adapter's limited implementation. It is not an independent hardware, release or end-to-end request proof unless its verifier actually performed those checks. A missing credential is “not checked”; an HTTP failure is “unavailable”; a checked contradiction is “rejected.” Legacy snapshots may have only a boolean and narrower error context.</p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Reference capture and continuity</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm">The publication probe makes bounded read-only HTTPS requests. Raw bodies are stored by SHA-256 and a derived latest index points to the last attempt and last success separately. Mirror comparison is byte agreement only. Changes in a public catalog's model or tier routing are distinct from volatile price text. The weekly model inventory is separate from the daily sentinel sample. Immutable events include route, old/new values, provenance and timestamp; no event is a deployment claim.</p>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm">Reproduce the public baseline with <code>python -m probes.references --catalogs</code>. No key is required for the reference sources. Catalog endpoints may accept an existing API key through environment variables; credentials are never written into observations.</p>

  <h2 id="cadence" class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Sampled identity cadence</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm">Daily probes can first see an existing fleet member. A value seen again can mean load balancing, rollback, recovery or sampling error. The table reports only observation windows; it does not estimate true rollout speed or fleet size.</p>
  <div class="mt-3 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white"><table class="w-full text-sm"><thead class="bg-slate-100 text-left"><tr><th class="p-2">Target</th><th class="p-2">Source type</th><th class="p-2">Samples</th><th class="p-2">Distinct identities</th><th class="p-2">Newly seen transitions</th><th class="p-2">Observed days per new identity</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  {% for item in quality.cadence %}<tr class="border-t border-slate-100"><td class="p-2 font-mono text-xs">{{ item.provider }}/{{ item.model }}</td><td class="p-2">{{ item.version_source }}</td><td class="p-2">{{ item.observations }}</td><td class="p-2">{{ item.distinct }}</td><td class="p-2">{{ item.novel }}</td><td class="p-2">{{ item.observed_days_per_new_identity if item.observed_days_per_new_identity is not none else "—" }}</td></tr>{% else %}<tr><td colspan="6" class="p-3">No identity series yet.</td></tr>{% endfor %}
  </tbody></table></div>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Current adapter check names</h2>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm">These field names help locate implementation and negative tests. Different architectures expose different checks, so a count of green cells is not a cross-provider privacy score.</p>
  <div class="mt-3 grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-2">{% for key, label in scorecard_labels.items() %}<div class="rounded border border-slate-200 bg-white p-2 text-xs"><strong>{{ label }}</strong> <code class="text-slate-500">{{ key }}</code></div>{% endfor %}</div>

  <p class="mt-8 text-sm">Read the <a class="underline" href="{{ repo_url }}research/review-2026-10-13/review.md">review and limitations</a> for the source-level concerns that motivated this structure, including quote binding, model-scoped policy, reply-key substitution and operator access paths.</p>
</section>
{% endblock %}
